      "options": [
        "Positive",
        "Negative",
        "Zero",
        "Depends on the focal length"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "Negative",
      "explanation": "In optical sign conventions, the object distance (u) is typically taken as negative when the object is real and placed in front of the lens."
    },
    {
      "question": "What happens to a ray of light that passes through the optical center of a lens?",
      "options": [
